IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr1-seat`

-- Cases for cr1-seat.l4: at least one case for each question, in the facts of a real person, and cases the
-- Regulations do not decide (asserted EQUALS NOTHING). Every expected value is written from the text of the
-- Regulations (C.R.C.-c.-385.txt) before the run. THE RATES, THE EXEMPTION AND THE EARNINGS CEILINGS ARE INVENTED
-- ROUND NUMBERS, NOT THE ACT'S FIGURES (the Act fixes them; piece cp1): rates 0.05 base, 0.01 first additional, 0.04
-- second additional; exemption 3,500; maximum pensionable earnings 70,000; additional maximum 80,000.

§ `Cases for the individual's questions`


§§ `A. What comes off my pay, and what my employer adds (regs 3 to 7)`

-- Priya is paid 6,000 monthly in 2024, has been paid 68,000 so far this year with nothing yet deducted, and has no provincial plan.
-- Base and first additional: 0.06 x (6,000 - 291.66) is cut by the room left (3,990); the second additional on the 2,000 above 70,000: worked out in the layer-1 tests (502.50).
#ASSERT `How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the Canada Pension Plan` 2024 0.05 0.01 0.04 3500 70000 80000 6000 6000 `paid monthly` 30 12 0 0 68000 FALSE 800 100 0.10 0.08 EQUALS JUST 502.50
-- The same pay in 2023: before 2024 there is no second additional contribution.
#ASSERT `How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the Canada Pension Plan` 2023 0.05 0.01 0.04 3500 70000 80000 6000 6000 `paid monthly` 30 12 0 0 68000 FALSE 800 100 0.10 0.08 EQUALS JUST 342.50
-- A provincial plan whose combined rate is nil: the Regulations do not say.
#ASSERT `How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the Canada Pension Plan` 2024 0.05 0.01 0.04 3500 70000 80000 3000 3000 `paid monthly` 30 12 0 0 10000 TRUE 800 100 0 0.08 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Amir is paid 3,000 monthly and nothing has yet been deducted: 0.06 x (3,000 - 291.66) = 162.50.
#ASSERT `How much will my employer deduct from this pay for the base and first additional contributions if nothing has yet been deducted this year` 0.05 0.01 3500 70000 3000 3000 `paid monthly` 30 12 EQUALS JUST 162.50
-- Whatever is deducted from the employee, the employer adds an equal amount.
#ASSERT `How much must my employer add from its own money for each deduction from my pay` 162.50 EQUALS JUST 162.50
-- 0.05 x 66,500 = 3,325; 0.01 x 66,500 = 665; 0.04 x 10,000 = 400.
#ASSERT `What is the most Canada Pension Plan contribution that can be deducted from my pay in a year` 0.05 0.01 0.04 3500 70000 80000 EQUALS 4390
#ASSERT `What is my basic exemption for each pay period` `paid monthly` 30 EQUALS 291.66
#ASSERT `What is my basic exemption for each pay period` `paid weekly` 7 EQUALS 67.30
-- Wages paid on a pay day.
#ASSERT `Is this pay ordinary remuneration for the Canada Pension Plan` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Director's fees where the corporation also pays other remuneration are not ordinary remuneration.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this pay ordinary remuneration for the Canada Pension Plan` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Director's fees where the corporation pays no other remuneration are.
#ASSERT `Is this pay ordinary remuneration for the Canada Pension Plan` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Yuki paid 590 in base contributions to a provincial plan at 5.9 per cent: on 10,000.
#ASSERT `How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the base contribution under a provincial pension plan` 590 0.059 EQUALS JUST 10000
-- A nil provincial rate: the Regulations do not say.
#ASSERT `How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the base contribution under a provincial pension plan` 590 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the first additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` 100 0.01 EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `How much of my pay counts as already contributed on for the second additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` 80 0.04 EQUALS JUST 2000

§§ `B. When my employer must remit, and who is treated as my employer (regs 8 to 8.3)`

#ASSERT `By what day must my employer remit what it took from this pay if it remits monthly` (YMD 2026 3 13) EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `Were the contributions taken from my pay remitted on time` (YMD 2026 4 14) (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`Were the contributions taken from my pay remitted on time` (YMD 2026 4 16) (YMD 2026 4 15))
-- Seven days after the employer ceases.
#ASSERT `My employer has stopped carrying on its business so by what day must it remit` (YMD 2026 6 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 17)
#ASSERT `Does my employer's payment come with a return in the prescribed form` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my employer's payment come with a return in the prescribed form` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the person who pays my wages treated as my employer` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the person who pays my wages treated as my employer` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `How much can the person treated as my employer recover from my actual employer` TRUE 1200 EQUALS JUST 1200
-- Not treated as the employer: the Regulations give no right of recovery.
#ASSERT `How much can the person treated as my employer recover from my actual employer` FALSE 1200 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `If the person treated as my employer fails to pay deduct or remit does Part I apply to them` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`If the person treated as my employer fails to pay deduct or remit does Part I apply to them` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is my mortgage a prescribed security interest` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my mortgage a prescribed security interest` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `How much can my prescribed security interest be` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE 500000 300000 50000 EQUALS JUST 150000
-- A failure before 2000: the text gives no rule.
#ASSERT `How much can my prescribed security interest be` (YMD 1999 12 31) TRUE 500000 300000 50000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does a kind of interest that I hold count as part of a prescribed security interest` `insurance or expropriation proceeds relating to land or a building that is the subject of a registered mortgage interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a kind of interest that I hold count as part of a prescribed security interest` `an assignment or hypothec of rents or of leases` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a kind of interest that I hold count as part of a prescribed security interest` `another interest` EQUALS NOTHING

